From a7e8ae5bc512947b3cdc2f589de67ccd6cf718ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:12:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/mips/mt7621: parallel NAND (NFI + ECC), NAND BootROM,
 locked L2 lines

- mt7621_nand.c: MT7621 NFI in PIO mode with a parallel SLC NAND
  (sector format 512 + 16, FDM registers, ECC always clean), backed by a
  folder of partition dumps; flash=nand, nand-id=
- BootROM for NAND boot: MediaTek NAND header, stage 1 in locked L2,
  return mailbox at 0xbe10ad00, then the bootloader to its load address
- L2 lines locked as SRAM kept apart from the DRAM (kseg0-only overlay),
  so the DDR init's memory tests do not overwrite the code running there
- 1004Kc without shadow register sets; GIC with 64 interrupts and its
  local interrupts masked after reset
